    <briefdescription>
<para>C++20 concept satisfied when a type is a framework expression type. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type to be checked.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>is_op</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> has the <computeroutput>op_type</computeroutput> member type alias of <computeroutput>detail::op</computeroutput>, either inherited from the <computeroutput>detail::op</computeroutput> base struct, or declared directly, like in <computeroutput>detail::value_base</computeroutput>, which avoids the empty base. It is used throughout the framework, both as a constraint and as a boolean expression in <computeroutput>if constexpr</computeroutput> contexts.</para>
<para>A custom comparator or operator uses it to tell the framework operands, like <computeroutput>to_i</computeroutput> or the <computeroutput>_i</computeroutput> literals, from the types of the application. The applications build their own expressions with <computeroutput>extension::compare_op</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>extension::predicate_op</computeroutput>, not by declaring the <computeroutput>op_type</computeroutput> marker, which the formatter could not report. </para>
